<title>TURKEY: CUKUROVA ELEKTRIK 9-MTH PROFITS SOAR.</title>
<headline>CUKUROVA ELEKTRIK 9-MTH PROFITS SOAR.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	7,724.02  vs   1,693.22</p>
<p>    Net profit			 3,862.01  vs     846.61</p>
<p>    Net sales			 20,109.08  vs   9,408.71</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 7,943.93  vs   2,682.93</p>
<p>    Exceptional income		 752.43  vs     754.64</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		591.44  vs     562.01</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    3,037.65  vs   1,753.37</p>
<p>    Total debts		     22,348.14  vs  15,211.82</p>
<p>    Equity			     5,903.45  vs   2,514.29</p>
<p>    Capital				500.00  vs     500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's biggest private sector utility Cukurova Elektrik A.S. produces and distributes power in southern Cukurova region. Its major shareholders are the Rumeli group run by the Uzan family.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
